-- title:
--   Places over ℚ̄ have open Galois stabilisers
-- statement:
--   Let $F$ be a field equipped with a $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra structure which is a curve over $\mathbb{Q}$ in the sense of the project's predicate `IsCurveOver` (every nonzero element of $F$ has a degree-zero divisor recording its order at every place, every place of $F/\mathbb{Q}$ has residue field finite over $\mathbb{Q}$, and $\Omega_{F/\mathbb{Q}}$ is free of rank one over $F$) and is essentially of finite type over $\mathbb{Q}$; let $\bar F$ be a field over $\bar{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` satisfying the same two conditions relative to $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$. Let $\mathrm{toBar} : F \to \bar F$ be a ring homomorphism compatible with $\mathbb{Q} \to \bar{\mathbb{Q}}$, such that the subfield of $\bar F$ generated by the images of $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$ and of $F$ is all of $\bar F$, and such that every finite subset of $F$ that is $\mathbb{Q}$-linearly independent has $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$-linearly independent image. Let $\mathrm{gal}$ be a monoid homomorphism from $\mathrm{Aut}_{\mathbb{Q}}(\bar{\mathbb{Q}})$ to the group of pairs $(\varphi, \tau) \in \mathrm{Aut}(\bar F) \times \mathrm{Aut}(\bar{\mathbb{Q}})$ with $\varphi$ semilinear over $\tau$, whose second component at $\sigma$ is $\sigma$ itself and whose action fixes $\mathrm{toBar}(x)$ for every $x \in F$. Then for every place $P$ of $\bar F/\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$ (a valuation subring of $\bar F$ containing the image of $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$, proper, and a principal ideal ring) there is an intermediate field $L$ of $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}$, finite-dimensional over $\mathbb{Q}$, such that every $\sigma$ fixing $L$ pointwise satisfies $\mathrm{gal}(\sigma) \cdot P = P$.
--
--   This is the statement that the Galois action on the places of a curve over $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$ obtained by base change from $\mathbb{Q}$ has open stabilisers. It supplies the continuity input for [`AlgebraicCurve.finite_pic0Torsion_and_exists_intermediateField_smul_eq_of_descent`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.finite_pic0Torsion_and_exists_intermediateField_smul_eq_of_descent), where a degree-zero divisor class is fixed by the intersection of the finitely many open subgroups attached to the places in its support.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_Place_exists_intermediateField_finiteDimensional_forall_smul_eq_of_descent.lean

